# ${project_name}

A small C11 command-line project with a reusable library boundary and CTest coverage.

## Build and test

Requirements: CMake 3.20+, Ninja, and a C11 compiler available in your shell.
On Windows with MSVC, run from a Developer PowerShell or Developer Command Prompt.

```sh
cmake --preset default
cmake --build --preset default
ctest --preset default
```

The executable is written to `build/${target_name}` (`build/${target_name}.exe` on Windows).

## Extend the project

Keep reusable code in `src/calculator.c` (public declarations in `include/`), and
command-line behavior in `src/main.c`. Add new source files to the library target
in `CMakeLists.txt`. Tests use explicit checks rather than `assert`, so they also
run in Release builds. The sample addition reports overflow without changing its
output argument; callers must check the returned boolean.
